<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down to 22.2 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down to 22.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 97 basis points to 22.20 percent, and rates also are seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters survey of eight Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     23.17	    22.20		   - 97 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     22.86	    22.43		   - 43 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    23.17	    22.74		   - 43 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     24.22	    23.87		   - 35 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local (0030 GMT).</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
